trace.content:
[THOUGHT] This is the final turn (16/16). HPV PCR testing was just requested but no result is available — and no further turns remain. The biopsy findings (nuclear hyperchromasia, multinucleation, increased mitoses in follicle-bearing epithelium) are pathognomonic for high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL/VIN 3), especially in the genital location. All major mimics have been systematically excluded:  
- Syphilis: RPR negative;  
- HIV-associated immunosuppression: HIV test negative;  
- Invasive SCC: no lymphadenopathy, and invasion would typically be noted in pathology if present;  
- Psoriasis/lichen planus: neither shows such severe cytologic atypia.  

HPV testing would strengthen causality — but the histopathologic diagnosis of HSIL is definitive *regardless of HPV status*, as per WHO classification. No additional test can be performed within turn limit.

[FINISH]

